# DESK31 item 2, coordinate probe: open C:\, then open C:\SUB in a SECOND
# window (Alt held over the double click -- `do_fopen`'s
# `(keystate & MODE_SCA) == MODE_ALT` new-window rule, desksupp.c:1130-1135),
# so the probe dump gives both windows' geometry.
#
# Dropping SUB on ITSELF cannot reach STILLDIR: `act_bdown` cancels a drop on
# the dragged item ("if ((wh == dst_wh) && (*pdobj == sobj)) dst_wh = NIL",
# deskact.c:666-670), which the first attempt at this gesture confirmed.  With
# TWO windows the handles differ, and dragging C:\SUB from the C:\ window into
# the C:\SUB window makes the destination C:\SUB\SUB -- `source_is_parent`.
100 parkbr
300 move 600 240
1000 arm
1200 mark A_IDLE
1600 move 38 35
1800 down
1803 up
1810 down
1813 up
2400 move 600 240
3200 mark B_WIN1
3400 move 515 103
3600 key 38
3800 down
3803 up
3810 down
3813 up
4000 key b8
4400 move 600 300
5400 mark C_WIN2
